                        "form": "most unessential"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e6969fc8-5da1-3ad7-b245-6ce014fac96c",
                        "entry_id": "3ad52503-edb7-3afa-8eeb-d645a6dcdcb4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Not essential."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "224f82a2-6ee2-48e5-9189-9d3e2817f05d",
                                "sense_id": "e6969fc8-5da1-3ad7-b245-6ce014fac96c",
                                "text": "1676, Joseph Glanvill, Seasonable Reflections and Discourses, London: R.W. [and] H. Mortlock, p. 92,\n[I] have a question more to ask you on occasion of what you have told me; and that is, Whether you are to leave every Minister and Church, as soon as any thing is said that is really erroneous, in the lesser and unessential matters?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ca167331-4ea8-4909-8bc6-7b30c7172ca9",
                                "sense_id": "e6969fc8-5da1-3ad7-b245-6ce014fac96c",
                                "text": "1716, Joseph Addison, The Free-Holder, No. 39, 4 May, 1716, London: D. Midwinter and J. Tonson, p. 225,\n[He was] moved rather with Pity than Indignation towards the Persons of those, who differed from him in the unessential Parts of Christianity."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2389074b-1ed4-4328-8900-054e229b3976",
                                "sense_id": "e6969fc8-5da1-3ad7-b245-6ce014fac96c",
                                "text": "“[…] strangeness is not in the nature of a thing, but in its relation to something extrinsic—in this case an unessential observer.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b145d52a-0528-413e-9b91-d579663090bb",
                                "sense_id": "e6969fc8-5da1-3ad7-b245-6ce014fac96c",
                                "text": "But all this part of it seemed remote and unessential."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e6fb59ed-666d-3925-b01f-ab08e0dfb050",
                        "entry_id": "3ad52503-edb7-3afa-8eeb-d645a6dcdcb4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Void of essence, or real being."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7b0e7297-6a2b-4927-9ed7-5113bd0e754e",
                                "sense_id": "e6fb59ed-666d-3925-b01f-ab08e0dfb050",
                                "text": "These [gates] past, if any pass, the void profound\nOf unessential Night receives him next\nWide gaping, and with utter loss of being\nThreatens him,"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1900cec7-5355-4579-8adb-6f6ece19dbc4",
                                "sense_id": "e6fb59ed-666d-3925-b01f-ab08e0dfb050",
                                "text": "[…] even before the Heavens, before those material Orbs, that now rowl over us, were call’d from the dark, and profound Abyss of unessential Nothing:"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
